    "[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m    \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mconsole\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34m.\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mlog\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m(\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mtest_data\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m,\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mlog_locals\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34m=\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;102;217;239;48;2;39;40;34mTrue\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m)\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                       \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                                                                  \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                                                                  \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mtest_log\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m(\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m)\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                                                        \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                                                                    \u{1b}[0m\n\nThe above produces the following output:                                                            \n\n🌆 \u{1b}]8;id=0;foo\u{1b}\\Log\u{1b}]8;;\u{1b}\\                                " +
    "                                                              \n\nNote the \u{1b}[1;36;40mlog_locals\u{1b}[0m argument, which outputs a table containing the local variables where the log    \nmethod was called.                                                                                  \n\nThe log method could be used for logging to the terminal for long running applications such as      \nservers, but is also a very nice debugging aid.                                                     \n\n\nYou can also use the builtin \u{1b}]8;id=0;foo\u{1b}\\\u{1b}[4;34mHandler class\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}]8;;\u{1b}\\ to format and colorize output from Python's logging      \nmodule. Here's an example of the output:                                                            \n\n🌆 \u{1b}]8;id=0;foo\u{1b}\\Logging\u{1b}]8;;\u{1b}\\                                                                                          \n\n\n\nTo insert an emoji in to console output place the name between two colons. Here's an example:       \n\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                                                                    \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34m>>\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34m>\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mconsole\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34m.\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mprint\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m(\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;230;219;116;48;2;39;40;34m\"\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;230;219;116;48;2;39;40;34m:smiley: :vampire: :pile_of_poo: :thumbs_up: :raccoon:\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;23" +
    "0;219;116;48;2;39;40;34m\"\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m)\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                       \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;237;0;126;48;2;30;0;16m😃\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;237;0;126;48;2;30;0;16m🧛\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;237;0;126;48;2;30;0;16m💩\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;237;0;126;48;2;30;0;16m👍\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;237;0;126;48;2;30;0;16m🦝\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                                                    \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                                                                    \u{1b}[0m\n\nPlease use this feature wisely.                                                                     \n\n\n\nRich can render flexible \u{1b}]8;id=0;foo\u{1b}\\\u{1b}[4;34mtables\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}]8;;\u{1b}\\ with unicode box characters. There is a large variety of formatting \noptions for borders, styles, cell alignment etc.                                                    \n\n🌆 \u{1b}]8;id=0;foo\u{1b}\\table movie\u{1b}]8;;\u{1b}\\                                                                                      \n\nThe animation above was generated with \u{1b}]8;id=0;foo\u{1b}\\\u{1b}[4;34mtable_movie.py\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}]8;;\u{1b}\\ in the examples directory.                    \n\nHere's a simpler table example:                                                                     \n\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                           " +
