    "                                                                                               \u{1b}[0m\n\nThe following screenshot is the output from the \u{1b}]8;id=0;foo\u{1b}\\\u{1b}[4;34mcolumns example\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}]8;;\u{1b}\\ which displays data pulled from an  \nAPI in columns:                                                                                     \n\n🌆 \u{1b}]8;id=0;foo\u{1b}\\columns\u{1b}]8;;\u{1b}\\                                                                                          \n\n\n\nRich can render \u{1b}]8;id=0;foo\u{1b}\\\u{1b}[4;34mmarkdown\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}]8;;\u{1b}\\ and does a reasonable job of translating the formatting to the terminal.   \n\nTo render markdown import the \u{1b}[1;36;40mMarkdown\u{1b}[0m class and construct it with a string containing markdown     \ncode. Then print it to the console. Here's an example:                                              \n\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                                                                    \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34mfrom\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mrich\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m.\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mconsole\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34mimport\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mConsole\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                                  \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34mfrom\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;" +
