    "4m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mlog_locals\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34m=\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;102;217;239;48;2;39;40;34mTrue\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m)\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m               \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                          \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                          \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mtest_log\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m(\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m)\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                            \u{1b}[0m\n\nThe above produces the following output:                    \n\n🌆 Log                                                      \n\nNote the \u{1b}[1;36;40mlog_locals\u{1b}[0m argument, which outputs a table         \ncontaining the local variables where the log method was     \ncalled.                                                     \n\nThe log method could be used for logging to the terminal for\nlong running applications such as servers, but is also a    \nvery nice debugging aid.                                    \n\n\nYou can also use the builtin \u{1b}[94mHandler class\u{1b}[0m                  \n(\u{1b}[4;34mhttps://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/logging.html\u{1b}[0m) to     \nformat and colorize output from Python's logging module.    \nHere's a" +
    "n example of the output:                            \n\n🌆 Logging                                                  \n\n\n\nTo insert an emoji in to console output place the name      \nbetween two colons. Here's an example:                      \n\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                            \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34m>>\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34m>\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mconsole\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34m.\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mprint\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m(\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;230;219;116;48;2;39;40;34m\"\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;230;219;116;48;2;39;40;34m:smiley: :vampire: :pile_of_poo: \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m      \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;230;219;116;48;2;39;40;34m:thumbs_up: :raccoon:\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;230;219;116;48;2;39;40;34m\"\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m)\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                   \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;237;0;126;48;2;30;0;16m😃\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;237;0;126;48;2;30;0;16m🧛\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;237;0;126;48;2;30;0;16m💩\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;237;0;126;48;2;30;0;16m👍\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;237;0;126;48;2;30;0;16m🦝\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                            \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                              " +
    "              \u{1b}[0m\n\nPlease use this feature wisely.                             \n\n\n\nRich can render flexible \u{1b}[94mtables\u{1b}[0m                             \n(\u{1b}[4;34mhttps://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/tables.html\u{1b}[0m) with    \nunicode box characters. There is a large variety of         \nformatting options for borders, styles, cell alignment etc. \n\n🌆 table movie                                              \n\nThe animation above was generated with \u{1b}[94mtable_movie.py\u{1b}[0m       \n(\u{1b}[4;34mhttps://github.com/textualize/rich/blob/main/examples/table\u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[4;34m_movie.py\u{1b}[0m) in the examples directory.                       \n\nHere's a simpler table example:                             \n\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                            \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34mfrom\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mrich\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m.\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mconsole\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34mimport\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mConsole\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                          \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34mfrom\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mrich\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m.\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mtable\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2" +
