    ";40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                          \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mconsole\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34m.\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mprint\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m(\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mtable\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m)\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                      \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                            \u{1b}[0m\n\nThis produces the following output:                         \n\n🌆 table                                                    \n\nNote that console markup is rendered in the same way as     \n\u{1b}[1;36;40mprint()\u{1b}[0m and \u{1b}[1;36;40mlog()\u{1b}[0m. In fact, anything that is renderable by  \nRich may be included in the headers / rows (even other      \ntables).                                                    \n\nThe \u{1b}[1;36;40mTable\u{1b}[0m class is smart enough to resize columns to fit the\navailable width of the terminal, wrapping text as required. \nHere's the same example, with the terminal made smaller than\nthe table above:                                            \n\n🌆 table2                                                   \n\n\n\nRich can render multiple flicker-free \u{1b}[94mprogress\u{1b}[0m              \n(\u{1b}[4;34mhttps://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/progress.html\u{1b}[0m) bars  \nto track long-running tasks.                                \n\nFor basic usage, wrap any sequence in the " +
    "\u{1b}[1;36;40mtrack\u{1b}[0m function and\niterate over the result. Here's an example:                 \n\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                            \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34mfrom\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mrich\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m.\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mprogress\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34mimport\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mtrack\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                           \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                          \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;102;217;239;48;2;39;40;34mfor\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mstep\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;255;70;137;48;2;39;40;34min\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mtrack\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m(\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;166;226;46;48;2;39;40;34mrange\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m(\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;174;129;255;48;2;39;40;34m100\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m)\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m)\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m:\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                            \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m    \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mdo_step\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;2" +
    "48;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m(\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34mstep\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[38;2;248;248;242;48;2;39;40;34m)\u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                         \u{1b}[0m\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m \u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                                            \u{1b}[0m\n\nIt's not much harder to add multiple progress bars. Here's  \nan example taken from the docs:                             \n\n🌆 progress                                                 \n\nThe columns may be configured to show any details you want. \nBuilt-in columns include percentage complete, file size,    \nfile speed, and time remaining. Here's another example      \nshowing a download in progress:                             \n\n🌆 progress                                                 \n\nTo try this out yourself, see \u{1b}[94mexamples/downloader.py\u{1b}[0m        \n(\u{1b}[4;34mhttps://github.com/textualize/rich/blob/main/examples/downl\u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[4;34moader.py\u{1b}[0m) which can download multiple URLs simultaneously   \nwhile displaying progress.                                  \n\n\n\nFor situations where it is hard to calculate progress, you  \ncan use the \u{1b}[94mstatus\u{1b}[0m                                          \n(\u{1b}[4;34mhttps://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/reference/console.htm\u{1b}[0m\n\u{1b}[4;34ml#rich.console.Console.status\u{1b}[0m) method which will display a  \n'spinner' animation and message. The animation won't prevent\nyou from using the console as normal. Here's an example:    \n\n\u{1b}[48;2;39;40;34m                                            " +
